---
title: Spheniscidae
---
# Spheniscidae

Spheniscidae holds all eighteen living penguin species, from the metre-tall
[[emperor-penguin]] to the little penguin of southern Australia. Prey is pursued
below the surface by the flippers alone, the feet and tail trailing behind as a
rudder, at speeds no other seabird sustains. Countershaded plumage conceals a
bird from above against the dark of the water and from below against the light
of the sky. Nearly all species breed colonially, and several fast for weeks at a
stretch while incubating.
